s 13 order fees, about 325. But each delivery covers two days, so roughly one day of stock stays overnight. That adds about 55 in storage per two-day cycle, around 700 in total, which outweighs the saving. Leftover stock carries over to later days in the daily plans anyway, so batching gives almost no extra protection against demand swings.\n\n**Candidates 0, 5 and 6.**\n- Candidate 5 orders about 1.05× the forecast all the way to the end, so it is likely to finish with unsold stock that is worth nothing.\n- Candidate 6 orders exactly the forecast. Since the multiplier averages 1.046, it runs short slightly more often.\n- Candidate 0 orders about 1.05× through the middle of the month and then cuts back to about 0.95× for the last orders (days 22–25). Its buffer stock covers those final days, so it sells it instead of writing it off at the end. That is the best trade-off between running short and having stock left over."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 358, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 358}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T03:06:12.340Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAraMwptSY6sF9FwWwWe"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018EQZBNm6899wrNJrjT96kb", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAraNNdTm2q5YT8RA4gA", "type": "message", "role": "assistant